<?xml version="1.0"?>
<clickhouse>
    <!-- Default query settings for every user that connects to the store.

         These two settings decide how much of ClickHouse's own diagnostic
         logging the store keeps, and they are the levers that actually stop
         the growth. Neither belongs in the system log sections of
         clickhouse-config.xml: both are query settings, and a query setting
         placed in a system log section is silently ignored.

         * log_processors_profiles writes a row for every processor of every
           query. The Usage console answers one range query with around
           forty ClickHouse queries, so this table grew to 8.3 GiB / 350M
           rows in two weeks and filled the disk. Nothing in AutoDev reads
           it; it is pipeline profiling for debugging a query, not a metric.

         * log_queries_min_query_duration_ms decides which queries reach
           query_log. Recording all of them filled query_log to 5.5 GiB /
           58M rows, almost all of them the console's own fast widget
           queries. The slow ones are the ones worth keeping.

         This file is mounted as a separate file in users.d on purpose: the
         image's entrypoint writes default-user.xml into that same directory
         with the generated password, and replacing that file would replace
         the password with it. ClickHouse merges every file in users.d, so
         this one only has to add the profiles it owns. -->
    <profiles>
        <default>
            <log_processors_profiles>0</log_processors_profiles>
            <log_queries_min_query_duration_ms>1000</log_queries_min_query_duration_ms>
        </default>
    </profiles>
</clickhouse>
